# Constants

A color, size, alpha, duration, or product limit that a person might tune belongs in one named place, and every use reads that name.

- Layout dp and sp: `ui/theme/Dimens.kt`
- Colors that are not Material roles: `ui/theme/WeatherColors.kt`
- Counts, weights, cache age, and scale limits: `weather/AppConfig.kt`
- Unit conversions and the length of an hour or day: `weather/Measures.kt`
- Date patterns: `ui/DateFormats.kt`

Material theme colors stay theme colors (`colorScheme`, `typography`). Do not copy them into the palette.

Leave a literal in place only when it is part of one formula and has no second meaning: a sunrise coefficient, a canvas coordinate inside a single drawing function, or a `0`/`1` bound. If the same number shows up twice, name it.

```kotlin
// Bad
Modifier.padding(12.dp)
Color(0xFF1565C0)

// Good
Modifier.padding(Dimens.cardPadding)
WeatherColors.rain
```
